WEBVTT

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.476
...people lived off the
fruit of the land.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:13.747
The seasonal produce was grown
where they were born and raised.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.271
Fruit of the land?

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.950
Be it watermelons or tomatoes...

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.215
...they are only at their best
for maybe a day.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.751
Only one day?

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.853
There's nothing like
freshly picked fruit.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.562
I'd love to try that.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:33.020
But the crows know
about this as well.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:36.569
They come when the
fruit is at its ripest.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.405
As for which one takes it sooner...

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.737
...it's up to whether the humans
or birds are wiser.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.934
But how do the birds know...

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:48.341
...when it's best to eat watermelon?

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.843
Who knows?

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.853
Maybe they're looking
for a change in color...

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:56.413
...or maybe they can smell it.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.491
Whatever the case...

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.926
...both the birds and watermelons...

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.862
...live on the same land
at the same time...

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.422
...so perhaps the birds
instinctively know.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.764
At the same time...

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.560
The here and now...?

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:14.969
The here and now, which includes
all of the past and the future.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:18.274
The past and the future?

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.981
Even in the smallest
of rice grains...

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.108
...a great deal of time is invested.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.353
The rice stalk that
produced the grain...

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:30.623
...and the time in which
its predecessors lived...

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.648
...and its predecessors...

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.096
...the insects, grass...

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.431
...soil, rain, and wind...

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.867
...all spending time, basking
in the light of the sun.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:46.363
The time flows...

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:47.972
...and I come into existence.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:52.009
Now, look at these green stalks.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:52.807
Huh?

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.316
The grains that will
become rice are there...

00:01:56.316 --> 00:02:01.754
...way at the bottom, slowly
taking form one at a time...

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:09.462
Such a small speck...

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.929
...within the leaves.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:16.463
Everything comes to life
from that state which is unseen.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.601
It's the same with human beings
like yourself.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.542
From way before you were born...

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:25.111
...when you were still inside your
mother's womb...

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:28.047
...the eggs that become the
next generation...

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:30.811
...were already within your
own body.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.549
From before I was born...

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:42.289
Episode 9: Before Birth

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:45.965
Reporting.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:49.769
After analyzing data from the
monitoring stations worldwide...

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.504
...as well as S. E. E. D.'s data...

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.507
...it is clear that there is a
definite organic connection...

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:57.210
...between the abnormality
in Earth's magnetic field...

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.379
...the unusual mantle convection...

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:02.549
...and the Van Allen Belt
microseismic phenomenon.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.584
You're not saying it's a pole shift?

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:07.485
Are you saying Earth's poles
are moving?

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:11.682
All the data seems to
point in that direction.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:14.661
But if a pole shift is happening...

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.362
...not only will that be the
end of civilization...

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.264
...but it'll also mean human
extinction.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.630
Can we trust that data?

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:24.728
Is it going to happen in time,
Chris?

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:28.065
The true awakening of the TI-2?

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:33.880
TI-2, Juna Ariyoshi...

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.850
...is in a state of great uncertainty
with respect to her TI abilities.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.551
In other words...

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.519
...the period of birthing pains.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.580
However, I will surely
lead her to an awakening... .

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.521
...even if it costs my own life.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:12.040
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:31.230
She decides what you should eat
and what you shouldn't eat.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:34.704
She doesn't know
how the food feels.

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.242
H-Hey...!

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:46.850
What?

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.488
What are you trying to pull?

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:53.121
You better not push yourself too
much and have another attack.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.965
I'm fine with just this
grapefruit juice.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:02.969
Just when Juna finally
agreed to eat regular food...

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:03.936
Sorry, sorry.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.699
I just feel kind of sick.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.974
My head feels like
It's going to explode.

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:10.310
You sure don't show me
much consideration.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.979
Always coming home
in the wee hours.

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:17.150
It's because you're so uptight
that Dad took off.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:17.912
Kaine!

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.859
You two are both so uptight.

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:01.156
Stop that.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:02.486
It hurts.

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:05.932
Come on.

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:08.601
I at least switched to
Miracle Lights.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:09.669
No.

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:14.800
I just heard the voice of a small
boy say "Stop that. It hurts."

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:16.642
Stop that!

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.303
You're creeping me out.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:22.148
"It hurts..."

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:24.810
Like a voice coming
from inside you.

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:54.113
Thanks.

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:56.249
I managed to make it on time.

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:58.444
Ah, it's nothing.

00:06:59.252 --> 00:06:59.852
Here.

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:00.787
Here's your lunch box.

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:02.922
I don't know how well
it turned out, but...

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:05.825
...I did include your favorite
fried chicken.

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:06.759
Wow.

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:09.629
You sure are considerate.

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:11.364
Well, I've got to go.

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:12.160
Right.

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:23.503
Juna!

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:44.764
I wonder what a high school girl
would be lamenting about...

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:46.732
...in the middle of the day.

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:48.693
What do you want?!

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:50.536
Did something happen again?!

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:54.768
Maybe you got dumped by your man
because you're always so edgy.

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.173
I'm going home!

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.502
Are you going to run away?

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:02.448
What is it today?

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:03.244
The Raaja?

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:06.111
Or did something happen
to Chris again?

00:08:06.586 --> 00:08:07.917
Don't worry.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.418
I'm just here on my own today.

00:08:10.723 --> 00:08:11.587
On your own?

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:21.560
What's this?!

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:27.270
You saved Chris that time
in the basement at S. E. E. D.

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:39.081
I figured I'd at least give you
a token of my appreciation.

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:52.598
No matter how dense
a girl you may be...

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:55.201
...you might as well have
a pretty handkerchief...

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:57.965
...to wipe away the tears
from a broken heart.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:58.795
How rude!

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:02.071
It's not like things between
Tokio and I are definitely over.

00:09:02.642 --> 00:09:04.906
Have you ever kissed him?

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:08.876
Uh, of course I have.

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:10.309
Did you slip him the tongue?

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:10.948
Huh?!

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:12.351
Well, uh...

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:14.478
Have you slept with him?

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:16.377
What... all of a sudden?!

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:18.587
I see.

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:20.549
I guess you haven't yet.

00:09:20.793 --> 00:09:21.487
Hey!

00:09:21.928 --> 00:09:24.063
Don't you be reading
my mind like that!

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.298
Besides...

00:09:25.298 --> 00:09:28.234
...I don't appreciate being talked
to like that by some kid!

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:32.330
Well, shall I tell you how
that would feel?

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:33.406
Huh?

00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:35.101
You're kidding! At your age?!

00:09:37.243 --> 00:09:39.545
I guess if I was dense like you...

00:09:39.545 --> 00:09:42.514
...I'd wonder what kind of
happy life I could have.

00:09:44.817 --> 00:09:45.909
Didn't I tell you?

00:09:46.719 --> 00:09:50.089
I can feel everything that
happens to me physically...

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:51.716
...before it actually happens.

00:09:52.358 --> 00:09:54.460
Like picking up someone's thoughts...

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:56.963
...and reading it like a
mystery novel...

00:09:56.963 --> 00:09:59.699
...only to be told part way
who the culprit is.

00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:00.666
It's the pits.

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:04.935
You feel it before it happens.

00:10:05.504 --> 00:10:06.973
That woman.

00:10:06.973 --> 00:10:10.409
She knew full well that
I was already in her womb...

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:13.901
...but she'd go off and sleep
with a different man every night.

00:10:15.615 --> 00:10:17.776
Why would she do such a thing?

00:10:19.852 --> 00:10:22.685
It's not like she even liked
any of them!

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.796
She'll think of things like what
clothes to wear the next day...

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:33.560
...or paying back her loan.

00:10:37.637 --> 00:10:40.906
She didn't even know
whose child I was!

00:10:40.906 --> 00:10:42.168
Why?!

00:10:50.583 --> 00:10:51.607
Why?!

00:10:52.051 --> 00:10:53.575
Why do I feel it so much?!

00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:58.445
Why is it that it feels so good?!

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:13.902
Don't tell me you're...

00:11:18.544 --> 00:11:22.181
I knew what it felt like
from before I was born.

00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:25.885
How could anyone expect that
I would grow up normally?

00:11:25.885 --> 00:11:26.874
But...

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:32.657
How could a baby in the womb
understand anything like that?

00:11:32.858 --> 00:11:34.260
If you think it's all a lie...

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.728
...then use the ears of your spirit
and listen in.

00:11:36.996 --> 00:11:39.089
Imagine that baby.

00:11:40.032 --> 00:11:41.863
You should be able to hear it, too.

00:11:42.435 --> 00:11:45.427
The voice of those babies' spirits.

00:11:46.072 --> 00:11:47.369
The spirits...

00:12:12.364 --> 00:12:15.925
Not yet, not yet, not yet...

00:12:16.235 --> 00:12:16.792
...not yet.

00:12:17.403 --> 00:12:18.665
I want to stay.

00:12:31.617 --> 00:12:35.519
Shima Hospital

00:12:37.389 --> 00:12:40.926
Doctor, we have the due date
for Mrs. Takeuchi in Room 307.

00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:42.528
Given the dilation of the cervix...

00:12:42.528 --> 00:12:45.929
...I would say it'll happen
early Saturday morning.

00:12:46.332 --> 00:12:47.594
Oh, I see.

00:12:49.001 --> 00:12:50.503
For the safety of the mother...

00:12:50.503 --> 00:12:52.671
...I think it's best to
deal with it earlier.

00:12:52.671 --> 00:12:53.739
I understand.

00:12:53.739 --> 00:12:56.675
Then I will administer
the labor inducement drug.

00:12:56.675 --> 00:12:58.438
Right. I'd appreciate that.

00:12:58.744 --> 00:13:00.541
No! No!

00:13:40.452 --> 00:13:42.288
Congratulations.

00:13:42.288 --> 00:13:44.256
She's a beautiful little girl.

00:13:56.168 --> 00:13:57.570
No.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:59.638
No, no, no, no.

00:13:59.638 --> 00:14:02.266
- No!
- 3160 grams.

00:14:02.541 --> 00:14:05.009
Now, let's clean you up a bit.

00:14:20.693 --> 00:14:24.151
Mom, Mom, Mom.

00:14:24.897 --> 00:14:25.693
Hold me.

00:14:27.533 --> 00:14:30.502
Hold me, hold me.

00:14:34.206 --> 00:14:38.540
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:42.982
Hey, did you know...

00:14:42.982 --> 00:14:46.785
...that babies don't cry much
when they're born?

00:14:46.785 --> 00:14:47.547
Huh?

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:49.385
They don't cry?

00:14:49.588 --> 00:14:50.213
That's right.

00:14:50.689 --> 00:14:53.392
When babies are born
through natural delivery...

00:14:53.392 --> 00:14:58.163
...they'll let out one gasp
in order to clear the windpipe...

00:14:58.163 --> 00:15:00.495
...but won't cry if they're
feeling secure.

00:15:02.701 --> 00:15:05.537
But that baby back there
was crying a lot.

00:15:05.537 --> 00:15:08.073
They get pulled out from
the warm womb...

00:15:08.073 --> 00:15:11.343
...dragged out under
the bright lights...

00:15:11.343 --> 00:15:14.471
...and get separated from
their mothers right away.

00:15:18.651 --> 00:15:20.175
Then, why do they?

00:15:20.386 --> 00:15:22.121
It's just the way it is.

00:15:22.121 --> 00:15:24.223
It's a common belief that a loud cry...

00:15:24.223 --> 00:15:27.283
...at birth is proof that the
baby's in good health.

00:15:28.961 --> 00:15:29.962
Besides...

00:15:29.962 --> 00:15:33.198
...a lot of babies wouldn't
have been born...

00:15:33.198 --> 00:15:35.098
...if hospitals didn't exist, after all.

00:15:39.939 --> 00:15:42.741
Well, modern people just
aren't capable of hearing...

00:15:42.741 --> 00:15:44.766
...the voices of the babies' feelings.

00:15:45.344 --> 00:15:46.011
But...

00:15:46.011 --> 00:15:48.070
...I heard the voice
of that baby before.

00:15:49.415 --> 00:15:52.282
No, no, no.

00:15:52.518 --> 00:15:54.386
128,000 yen!

00:15:54.386 --> 00:15:56.911
How can I come up
with that kind of money?

00:16:04.029 --> 00:16:04.825
Kaine?

00:16:06.832 --> 00:16:07.662
Which means...!

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:11.060
No, no, no.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.803
What are you going to do?

00:16:13.072 --> 00:16:15.336
Your silly sister.

00:16:15.541 --> 00:16:18.066
The baby inside of her
is calling.

00:16:20.813 --> 00:16:24.909
Mom, mom, mom.

00:16:27.619 --> 00:16:29.951
You can hear it, too, can't you?!

00:16:41.433 --> 00:16:42.058
Juna!

00:16:42.401 --> 00:16:44.232
What are you doing here?!

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:45.894
Don't...

00:16:46.338 --> 00:16:48.499
...don't you get an abortion!

00:16:48.974 --> 00:16:52.211
The baby within you is
calling out "Mom! Mom!"

00:16:52.211 --> 00:16:54.042
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:16:55.748 --> 00:16:58.273
What a fool. No tact at all.

00:16:58.751 --> 00:17:02.414
I don't need to have a kid like you
talk to me like that!

00:17:04.356 --> 00:17:05.414
Uh, but...

00:17:05.691 --> 00:17:07.860
I don't know who you
heard it from...

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:10.129
...but how can you expect me
to have the child...

00:17:10.129 --> 00:17:11.460
...of a guy I don't even love?!

00:17:12.598 --> 00:17:14.327
You don't even love him?

00:17:15.367 --> 00:17:16.766
Just leave me alone!

00:17:37.322 --> 00:17:38.346
Thanks for waiting.

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.269
Hey, Tokio...

00:17:57.843 --> 00:18:00.712
...you want to go see Hirotsugu
Mochida in concert next time?

00:18:00.712 --> 00:18:03.738
Or maybe you'd like
Kana Yumeno instead?

00:18:16.762 --> 00:18:18.389
At the hospital...

00:18:20.299 --> 00:18:22.164
You heard it as well, right?

00:18:22.534 --> 00:18:25.298
The feelings of a baby
before she's born.

00:18:26.705 --> 00:18:28.070
Before she's born?

00:18:28.707 --> 00:18:29.741
Of course...

00:18:29.741 --> 00:18:32.911
...a baby doesn't use words
to explain how she feels.

00:18:32.911 --> 00:18:37.905
We're just able to translate that
baby's feelings into words.

00:18:38.484 --> 00:18:40.076
But didn't you hear it like this?

00:18:40.552 --> 00:18:41.814
Not yet.

00:18:42.654 --> 00:18:43.279
That's right.

00:18:43.722 --> 00:18:45.622
She wanted to stay longer.

00:18:46.492 --> 00:18:47.618
Why do you think?

00:18:47.759 --> 00:18:48.817
I don't know.

00:18:49.161 --> 00:18:50.526
How am I supposed to know?

00:18:51.029 --> 00:18:52.698
You know...

00:18:52.698 --> 00:18:55.132
...babies can decide
for themselves...

00:18:55.334 --> 00:18:58.737
...when they want to
be born into this world.

00:18:58.737 --> 00:18:59.795
No way.

00:19:00.205 --> 00:19:02.366
Can babies really do that?

00:19:05.611 --> 00:19:10.742
A baby can feel everything in
the little ocean that is the womb.

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:14.280
Whether it be the mother's voice,
or heart beat.

00:19:14.486 --> 00:19:17.222
What she's eating,
or what she's drinking.

00:19:17.222 --> 00:19:20.125
Whether she's laughing
or whether she's sad.

00:19:20.125 --> 00:19:24.585
A baby can also feel the tides
and the phases of the moon.

00:19:25.264 --> 00:19:27.858
And then it decides it
wants to be born.

00:19:28.167 --> 00:19:31.466
It sends a message with its heart
and with its hormones.

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:35.428
Why is it that
the mother can't feel that?

00:19:35.807 --> 00:19:38.833
Why can't the mother understand
what the baby is feeling?

00:19:39.645 --> 00:19:41.078
Chris said...

00:19:42.181 --> 00:19:44.249
...that everyone does feel it.

00:19:44.249 --> 00:19:46.985
But the clutter of words and
knowledge interferes...

00:19:46.985 --> 00:19:49.283
...and they're not able to hear it.

00:19:49.521 --> 00:19:50.579
No...

00:19:52.124 --> 00:19:53.926
Chris' mother and father...

00:19:53.926 --> 00:19:56.326
...were both archaeologists.

00:19:56.728 --> 00:19:58.286
Chris' parents?

00:19:59.097 --> 00:20:02.167
While they were exploring
the world...

00:20:02.167 --> 00:20:06.305
...digging up sites and decoding
ancient scripts and such...

00:20:06.305 --> 00:20:08.607
...they realized that the
ancient people...

00:20:08.607 --> 00:20:11.599
...were far more aware
of things than we are.

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:14.246
They realized that those
people felt the spirits...

00:20:14.246 --> 00:20:16.915
...of plants and animals, water...

00:20:16.915 --> 00:20:22.376
...wind, and even rocks, and
of course the baby in the womb.

00:20:24.056 --> 00:20:26.692
It was then that Chris' mother...

00:20:26.692 --> 00:20:29.795
...while she was living on a
small island in the South Pacific...

00:20:29.795 --> 00:20:34.823
...heard Chris' words before he
was born from within her womb.

00:20:36.768 --> 00:20:38.167
Chris' words?

00:20:39.204 --> 00:20:40.398
What'd he say?

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:42.104
To the sea.

00:20:43.175 --> 00:20:44.107
To the sea...

00:21:13.272 --> 00:21:18.733
Cinq, quatre, trois, deux, un...

00:21:19.645 --> 00:21:20.373
...now!

00:21:36.561 --> 00:21:38.825
Happy birthday.

00:21:40.365 --> 00:21:44.028
When people are born
into this world...

00:21:45.037 --> 00:21:47.403
That's why Chris is so gentle.

00:21:47.706 --> 00:21:49.867
He understands what true love is.

00:21:58.183 --> 00:22:01.720
Hey, do you really like that guy?

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:04.056
Uh, well...

00:22:04.056 --> 00:22:05.284
...sure I do...

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:06.718
Probably...

00:22:07.893 --> 00:22:10.327
Then why haven't you
gone past kissing?

00:22:10.629 --> 00:22:11.789
Uh, well...

00:22:13.899 --> 00:22:14.800
Oh, boy.

00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:17.502
You sure are a true Japanese.

00:22:17.502 --> 00:22:20.472
You shouldn't have to worry
too much about size.

00:22:20.472 --> 00:22:21.506
But, well...

00:22:21.506 --> 00:22:24.339
...Tokio likes big breasts, and...

00:22:26.244 --> 00:22:29.042
...well, I've never done it.

00:22:29.815 --> 00:22:31.683
I wouldn't like it if it hurt...

00:22:31.683 --> 00:22:34.982
...and, besides, what if
I get pregnant at my age?

00:22:41.259 --> 00:22:45.491
But, I was once ready to do it.

00:22:57.609 --> 00:22:58.910
If back then...

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:01.572
...I didn't run into that Raaja...

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:04.374
...and if I hadn't met you...

00:23:04.516 --> 00:23:07.076
...Tokio wouldn't be...

00:23:07.786 --> 00:23:09.413
...so turned off by me...

00:23:11.123 --> 00:23:13.825
Boy, you sure are dense.

00:23:13.825 --> 00:23:15.127
What'd you want?!

00:23:15.127 --> 00:23:17.529
Why don't you go and
find out for sure?

00:23:17.529 --> 00:23:18.962
How he really feels about you.

00:23:20.465 --> 00:23:22.033
Not with words...

00:23:22.033 --> 00:23:23.125
...but with your heart.

00:23:26.972 --> 00:23:28.707
I really enjoyed myself today.

00:23:28.707 --> 00:23:30.299
Well, good luck.

00:23:33.945 --> 00:23:35.173
- Um...
- Huh?

00:23:35.747 --> 00:23:36.304
Oh, excuse me!

00:23:52.831 --> 00:23:54.232
Hey, Oshima...

00:23:54.232 --> 00:23:56.001
...how about some
karaoke tonight?

00:23:56.001 --> 00:23:58.526
There's a really good place
near Toa Road.

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:00.032
Huh...

00:24:00.639 --> 00:24:01.673
Come on.

00:24:01.673 --> 00:24:05.666
All you have to say
is "Huh... Huh..."

00:24:06.611 --> 00:24:07.134
Huh...

00:24:08.346 --> 00:24:09.711
Oh, nevermind.

00:24:11.283 --> 00:24:14.741
I was ready for a
long-running battle.

00:24:22.527 --> 00:24:24.119
See you later.

00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:25.564
Huh?

00:24:25.564 --> 00:24:26.364
Uh, hey!

00:24:26.364 --> 00:24:27.265
Wait!

00:24:27.265 --> 00:24:28.664
Sayuri!

00:25:22.821 --> 00:25:23.955
Tokio...

00:25:23.955 --> 00:25:25.183
Juna...

00:25:43.608 --> 00:25:45.803
Let's go to the sea.

00:25:46.177 --> 00:25:46.768
Huh?

00:25:47.579 --> 00:25:48.409
Not this one.

00:25:50.148 --> 00:25:51.274
But the real sea.

00:26:31.623 --> 00:26:32.988
Uh, um...

00:26:33.625 --> 00:26:37.061
Nothing happened between
me and Sayuri.

00:26:37.529 --> 00:26:41.090
Last night, we just went to
karaoke until midnight...

00:26:56.348 --> 00:26:59.374
I can feel it now...

00:27:00.018 --> 00:27:03.784
The sea that lies within me.

00:27:06.224 --> 00:27:07.418
The sea, huh?

00:27:30.515 --> 00:27:31.650
Don't come!

00:27:31.650 --> 00:27:34.285
I won't make good company now!

00:27:34.285 --> 00:27:36.913
I'm looking my worst
right now!

00:27:43.395 --> 00:27:46.865
I didn't want you
to be taken away.

00:27:46.865 --> 00:27:51.268
I didn't want her feelings to
shift toward you anymore!

00:27:53.805 --> 00:27:55.397
You can cry, you know.

00:27:55.540 --> 00:27:57.735
That's what a human does.

00:28:02.747 --> 00:28:04.271
Why?

00:28:04.416 --> 00:28:07.351
Why are you so kind, Chris?

00:28:07.952 --> 00:28:09.749
Why?

00:28:18.363 --> 00:28:20.263
I'm sorry, I...

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:25.036
...I'm sorry, at such
a crucial moment.

00:28:25.036 --> 00:28:26.604
I...

00:28:26.604 --> 00:28:28.367
It's more than enough.

00:28:28.640 --> 00:28:32.371
Your feelings are more than enough.

00:28:32.744 --> 00:28:34.234
I'm so sorry.

00:28:42.387 --> 00:28:43.376
Mom...

00:28:44.656 --> 00:28:46.021
Mom...

00:28:47.559 --> 00:28:48.924
Mom...

00:28:52.397 --> 00:28:54.865
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:28:59.270 --> 00:29:05.175
Tooku naru yubisaki megakete

00:29:06.344 --> 00:29:11.916
Nandomo nandomo namae yobu

00:29:11.916 --> 00:29:17.855
Toki wo sora wo koete anata wo

00:29:18.990 --> 00:29:26.089
Mamotteiru to tsutaetai no

00:29:29.400 --> 00:29:34.739
Hiyayaka na kuuki mo

00:29:34.739 --> 00:29:38.197
Mune no oku yadotta

00:29:38.710 --> 00:29:47.185
Netsu wa ubaenai tatoe ima wa mada

00:29:47.185 --> 00:29:56.060
Chisakute hakanai ai deshika nakutemo

00:29:56.060 --> 00:30:02.192
Tooku naru yubisaki megakete

00:30:03.101 --> 00:30:08.840
Nandomo nandomo namae yobu

00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:14.608
Toki wo sora wo koete anata wo

00:30:15.914 --> 00:30:23.753
Mamotteiru to tsutaetai no

00:30:38.903 --> 00:30:41.337
You should go home, Tokio.

00:30:42.740 --> 00:30:45.038
Is some monster going to
come after this place?

00:30:47.846 --> 00:30:49.939
So, am I in the way then?

00:30:52.650 --> 00:30:55.813
Hey, you want to come to
my place tonight?

00:31:00.525 --> 00:31:02.356
Genetic engineering...?

00:31:04.529 --> 00:31:06.087
You must've loved him.

00:31:09.300 --> 00:31:11.768
Sometimes loving someone
doesn't make any difference.

00:31:12.303 --> 00:31:14.931
Modern civilization is
a pile of garbage.

00:31:16.407 --> 00:31:18.272
So, I'm in the way.

00:31:24.883 --> 00:31:25.917
It's begun.

00:31:25.917 --> 00:31:26.747
Begun?

00:31:32.624 --> 00:31:34.956
You're wrong, Tokio.

00:31:38.129 --> 00:31:41.223
Will you not understand until
the world is destroyed?

00:31:45.303 --> 00:31:47.272
Episode 10: The Flickering Genes

00:31:47.272 --> 00:31:53.268
Episode 11: The Day of No Return
